{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773865413,"nonce":"mngkoPj8WSsnlUtpsp8h4h4NhTQ=","title":"Add Claude Agent SDK backend to Console (alongside PTY)","message":"Introduce an abstract AgenticBackend interface for Console sessions, with two concrete implementations: PTYBackend (existing node-pty path) and SDKBackend (new, using @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk).\n\nWhen creating a new Console session, the user selects the backend (PTY or SDK). PTY remains fully functional as a fallback; SDK is the forward path for Claude sessions.\n\nThe SDK backend enables:\n- Hook interception (PreToolUse, PostToolUse, SubagentStart/Stop, etc.) wired to Mandible policy\n- Permission requests surfaced as Mandible dashboard dialogs rather than terminal prompts\n- Real-time structured event stream (no ANSI stripping, no ring buffer, no line-buffer heuristics)\n- Session lifecycle owned by Mandible from creation (session ID known at spawn time, not discovered from JSONL)\n- Multi-model support (model selection native to SDK query options)\n\nRelated bugs:\n- 3da19be: model/hyperparam controls — SDK backend makes this clean (pass model in query options)\n- 781f473: subagent result pruning — PostToolUse hook is the intervention point\n- aea2c67: prompt input bar (closed/merged) — SDK backend provides a cleaner foundation\n\nPTY backend is vestigial once SDK is stable; keep both until confidence is established. The abstraction (AgenticBackend interface) is the primary design artifact — getting the interface right while maintaining both implementations ensures the abstractions are correct before removing PTY.","files":null}]}